headers {
  x-api-key: {{process.env.TOLLGURU_API_KEY}}
}

tests {
  // TollGuru answers {"status":"OK", ...} on success and an error message otherwise.
  test("status is OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus(), JSON.stringify(res.getBody())).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody().status, JSON.stringify(res.getBody())).to.equal("OK");
  });
}

docs {
  # TollGuru Toll API (v2)

  Direct calls to TollGuru (not a Vahn service), the provider behind plutus-java's
  `TollGuruClient` (ENG-1313). plutus-java uses it for the FASTag estimate when
  `tollEstimate.primaryStrategy` is `TOLLGURU`, with the key from the `TOLLGURU_API_KEY` env var.

  ## Credentials and inputs

  Read from `bruno/collections/tollguru/.env` (gitignored). Create it locally:

  ```
  TOLLGURU_API_KEY=<tollguru api key>
  # optional: price a specific route, e.g. a trip's encoded_polyline from plutus
  TOLLGURU_POLYLINE=<google encoded polyline>
  ```

  Route endpoints and vehicle type are plain vars in `environments/staging.bru`
  (default: Gurugram → Jaipur on NH48, `3AxlesTruck`, the type plutus sends for VC7/VC10/VC11).

  ```bash
  npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/collections/tollguru --env staging
  ```

  Every request is billed against the TollGuru plan; the folder run makes two calls.
}
